  "description": "Vectors for draft-mih-sokolov-cose-deterministic-encodings. Header label 271 is the value the draft suggests for TBD_1; it is not assigned. 'protected' is the serialized protected header map. An 'encoding' member is a value of the COSE Deterministic Encodings registry; an emit case without one uses value 1. A verifier holding 'value_cbor' decodes it and re-creates the preimage; one holding 'preimage' hashes it. An 'emit_reject' case is a value the encoding cannot encode: a producer emits no envelope for it. A 'conformance' case is stored content checked before hashing: 'recreated' is what the encoding produces for the decoded value (null when the value is outside the encoding), and the content conforms exactly when 'recreated' equals 'preimage'.",
